course: dictionary
lesson: 168
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. «An estate agent helps sell houses and shows people round.» Here an agent is a person whose job is to act for someone else, not a spy.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The secret agent crept past the guards» tells you agent means a spy, because secret and crept are the clues. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence best? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: Science uses agent in a different way. An agent is something that causes a change. «Running water is the most powerful agent of erosion on Earth» means running water is the thing that wears the land away. Baking powder is a raising agent because it makes a cake rise.
fact: An agent can be a person who acts for someone else, such as a travel agent or an estate agent.
fact: A secret agent is a spy who works secretly for a country.
fact: In science, an agent is something that causes a change, such as a cleaning agent or a raising agent.
fact: A free agent is someone who can do what they like and is not tied to anyone.
fact: Estate agent is the UK word; in the USA people say real estate agent.
exercise: «An estate agent helps sell houses and shows people round.» What is an estate agent? | A person who can do what they like | *A person whose job is to act for someone, helping to sell houses | A secret spy who works for a country | Something that makes a cake rise
exercise: «Running water is the most powerful agent of erosion on Earth.» In this sentence, what is an agent? | A cake ingredient | *Something that causes a change, here wearing away the land | A spy | A person who sells houses
exercise: Mia says baking powder is a raising agent. What does raising agent mean? | *Something that makes a cake rise | A spy who works at night | A person who raises money for charity | A free person with no job
test: «The secret agent crept quietly past the guards.» What is the agent in this sentence? | A football player's agent | A cleaning agent for the floors | *A spy who works secretly for a country | A travel agent booking holidays
test: Which sentence uses agent to mean something that causes a change? | A free agent can do what they like | *Lemon juice is a cleaning agent that shines the tiles | The estate agent showed us round the house | A travel agent booked our holiday
exam: Jo says a free agent is a spy. What does free agent mean? | A spy working for a country | A person who sells houses | *Someone who can do what they like and is not tied to anyone | A cake ingredient
